ISO-only delivery workflow verification, 2026-11-15 UTC

The unchanged final optical ISO was used in every run:
SHA256 6af39753816e30ab40e77cf56af4a8edce4de20abb30ef09d722884c217a5f3b
QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,128MiB, SeaBIOS and standard VGA. The ISO is read-only
on IDE index2. No prebuilt user-data image is required or distributed by this
workflow. The test-only blank-disk fixture is private and extensionless.

1. Optical ISO alone, no ATA hard disk: PASS
Boot reaches the visible graphical zero> prompt within40 seconds. disks
reports No supported ATA volumes. Optical media are not writable volumes.
create test and watch refuse unavailable volume access; format ZERO refuses
because no real dedicated raw ZeroFS volume is selected. Every command
returns to the prompt, and info/tasks show live graphics/compute workers.
The only attached medium is the read-only optical ISO; there is no writable
hard-disk target. nodisk/first.png was visually inspected. The VM was stopped.

2. Newly created blank16MiB virtual hard disk: PASS
The host created a fresh zero-filled file blank/blank-disk solely for this
test and attached it as ATA IDE primary master. The ISO remains optical.
disks initially reports A:| disk0 16MiB unknown. create before is refused;
the entire disk checksum remains exactly its initial zero-filled value,
recorded in before-format.sha256 and preformat-unchanged.txt. Discovery does
not automatically format or initialize the new disk.

The explicit commands then succeed:
 format ZERO
 disks
 create hello
 save hello Zero ISO disk persistence
 read hello
 watch
disks now identifies A:| as ZeroFS; read returns the exact saved text and
watch lists hello. All three mutations report Saved to disk. info/tasks
remain available. After VM shutdown every byte beyond the first18 sectors
still equals the original zero-filled disk. blank/first.png was inspected.

3. Full new-process restart with that same disk: PASS
The first VM process exited before a second QEMU process started. No disk
fixture was copied, reset or reformatted. Startup mounts ZeroFS; disks lists
the16MiB volume; read hello returns Zero ISO disk persistence and watch lists
hello. A whole-disk checksum comparison with the post-write image passes,
so this read-only restart leaves the persistent image unchanged. See
blank/restart.serial, restart.png and restart-unchanged.txt. The second
process was stopped after the screen was inspected.

Reproduction and preservation
run.sh records exact VM options, boot deadlines, keyboard injection and all
assertions. Per-scenario command files, serial logs, QEMU logs and screenshots
are retained. The default run deliberately refuses to overwrite a preexisting
blank-disk fixture; the restart subcommand reuses only the test-created file.
original-inputs.sha256 records unchanged build/data.img,build/data.vdi and
both final ISO copies. No implementation source or existing user-data disk
was modified. All three test VM processes have stopped.
This is BIOS64 QEMU workflow evidence; native VirtualBox is not claimed.
